        "original_id": "011fdbf9-f172-58c1-97d3-16a1ad56b5b9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Dahlia, Aruncus, Butea, Coreopsis, Toxicodendron vernicifluum\n- Chemicals: Butein\n- Concepts: plant genera, herbaceous perennials, native range, biological effects\n\nFacts:\n- Dahlia is a genus of bushy, tuberous, herbaceous perennial plants native to Mexico.\n- Aruncus is a genus of clump-forming herbaceous perennial plants in the family Rosaceae.\n- Butein can be found in Toxicodendron vernicifluum, formerly called Rhus verniciflua.\n- Butein can be found in Dahlia, Butea monosperma in the genus Butea, and Coreopsis.\n- Butein has antioxidative, aldose reductase inhibitory, and advanced glycation endproducts inhibitory effects.",
